- The CMU Pronouncing Dictionary (assets/lexicon/pron.lex, repacked): Carnegie Mellon University
  and the cmudict contributors, BSD-style licence (assets/lexicon/cmudict-LICENSE.txt).
- WordNet 3.1 (assets/lexicon/wordnet.lex, pruned): Princeton University, WordNet 3.1 licence
  (assets/lexicon/wordnet-LICENSE.txt).
- DeepFilterNet 3 ONNX model (crates/ml/assets/DeepFilterNet3_onnx.tar.gz): Hendrik Schroeter,
  MIT OR Apache-2.0.
- DAWproject test projects (crates/engine/tests/fixtures/dawproject/bitwig-*.xml, test data
  only): Bitwig GmbH, MIT.
- The egui default fonts (Ubuntu-Light: Ubuntu Font Licence 1.0; Hack: MIT; Noto Emoji: OFL-1.1;
  emoji-icon-font: OFL-1.1/MIT) ship inside the egui crate under their own licenses.

Everything else bundled is original: icons drawn in code, demo audio synthesised in code, and the
owner's own work (the FreeDAWm logo, wordmark and splash, the FireStation factory presets, the
Band library and the amp cabinet impulse responses in assets/amp-irs/), all released under the
MIT License.

Third-party ML models that some features download (separation, karaoke, transcription) are not
bundled: the app fetches them from their authors' own pages, and each one's licence is shown in
the app (Setup > ML Models) and listed in ATTRIBUTION.md. Some of them state no licence.

Rust crate dependencies are under their own licenses (see Cargo.lock; `cargo about` or
`cargo deny check licenses` lists them).
